# Startup Issue Fix Walkthrough

I have investigated the "doesn't open" issue and made the following fixes.

## Changes

### Fixed Missing Import
The [reproduce_issue.js](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/reproduce_issue.js) script was failing because [layoutGenerator.js](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/%E6%BC%AB%E7%94%BB/src/utils/manga/layoutGenerator.js) had been moved to `src/utils/manga/`. I updated the import path.

- **File**: `reproduce_issue.js`
- **Change**: Updated import to `src/utils/manga/layoutGenerator.js`

### Fixed Runtime Error
I found a critical bug in `src/hooks/useLayoutGeneration.js` where an undefined variable `actualPages` was being used. This would cause the application to crash when generating a layout.

- **File**: `src/hooks/useLayoutGeneration.js`
- **Change**: Replaced `actualPages` with `finalPages`.

## Verification Results

### Build Verification
Ran `npm run build` and it completed successfully.

### Reproduction Script
Ran `node reproduce_issue.js` and it now passes successfully, confirming the core layout generation logic is working.

